//? Title: Inception v4 and Inception-ResNet: Complete Depth and Scaled Branches
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Combining wide Inception branches with residual addition introduces a scale choice: how
large should each learned correction be relative to its identity path? We check residual
values and gradients directly, preserve complete reference block counts, and show both compact
models learning through explicit tensor Adam loops with paired parameter/state checkpoints.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.2_classic_architectures/inception_v4_resnet.cpp`.

> The method

Inception v4 repeats A/B/C blocks 4/7/3 times between its stem and two reductions.
Inception-ResNet-v2 repeats 10/20/10, retaining the full depth even in the CPU demonstration.
Its branch outputs are concatenated, projected by a biased linear 1×1 filter without BN,
scaled, then added to the input. Other convolutions use beta-only BN/ReLU. The ordinary
residual scales are .17, .10 and .20 for A/B/C; the final C block instead uses scale one
and omits its final ReLU, following TF-Slim. Main dropout retains .8; the auxiliary head
precedes the second reduction. He initialization and eager unbiased-variance moving updates
are explicit library adaptations.

Without the final ReLU, a block is y=x+sF(x;theta), so

$$
\frac{\partial y}{\partial x}=I+s\frac{\partial F}{\partial x},\qquad
\frac{\partial y}{\partial\theta}=s\frac{\partial F}{\partial\theta}.
$$
\alttext(The input derivative retains an identity term while branch parameter derivatives are multiplied by the residual scale.)

The fixture shares weights across scales zero, s and 2s. It checks exact identity at zero,
linear output/parameter-gradient scaling and the identity contribution to input gradients
for all three branch types. Final ReLU is disabled only for this algebraic diagnostic; normal
blocks still apply it. A later gate can change which derivatives survive. These equalities
explain the scale mechanism without proving stability or faster learning on arbitrary data.

Full forward checks use 299 pixels and 1000 classes, validating every named stage and the
following learned/main, auxiliary and moving-state counts:

| Model | Main learned scalars | Auxiliary learned scalars | BN moving scalars |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| Inception v4 | 42648232 | 3358568 | 64960 |
| Inception-ResNet-v2 | 55813192 | 3366760 | 62336 |

Convolution work is the sum over branches of O(NHoWo kh kw Cin Cout); pointwise residual
projection adds O(NHW Cbranch Cin), and repeated blocks multiply these costs. The full
forward checks omit backward storage. Compact graphs separately check gradients through every
learned tensor while retaining all blocks, the final C exception and the auxiliary head.

The CIFAR-10 runs use 107-pixel bilinear inputs, one-eighth widths, BN momentum .9, 128
fitting/64 validation/64 official-test images, batch eight and 10 epochs (kept short so
both fits run in seconds). The written-out
objective contains .1-smoothed main CE, .4 times smoothed auxiliary CE, and kernel L2=.0001/2.
Adam(.001) updates learnable tensors; BN moving state updates during the forward pass. Only
unsmoothed primary validation NLL selects a paired parameter/state checkpoint. Augmentation
uses independent padded crops/flips. These different architectures are not a controlled
residual ablation or ImageNet reproduction. Cached CIFAR-10 is required.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/inception_v4_resnet_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/inception_v4_resnet_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/inception_v4_resnet_concept.tikz > build/inception_v4_resnet_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/inception_v4_resnet_concept.svg build/inception_v4_resnet_concept.dvi > build/inception_v4_resnet_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
